# Who GitHub requests a review from, per path. One entry, because the repository has one maintainer:
# every path is owned by the same person, and a narrower rule would only claim a structure that does
# not exist yet. Add paths above the catch-all as teams take ownership of them -- the last matching
# pattern wins, so a specific rule has to come after `*`, not before it.
#
# An email address rather than `@mohammaddaoudfarooqi`, which is the same account. GitHub resolves an
# address to the account that has it, so the two are equivalent as long as the address stays on the
# account and the account keeps write access here. Switch to the handle if a review request ever fails
# to route: the handle depends on neither of those conditions.
#
# This file assigns reviewers. It does not require them -- that is branch protection, which lives in
# repository settings rather than in the tree, and without it the assignment is a suggestion.
* mohammaddaoud.farooqi@mongodb.com
